--!strict
-- Every sound Vellum plays. Pure data keyed by sfx id, the seam between the audio generators and the
-- client, the way AssetIds is for the textures.
--
-- Each entry names the WAV in assets/audio/ it is the upload of, the length of that file as read from
-- its header (tests/SoundConfig.spec.luau holds the two together), the volume and speed it plays at, and
-- how much its pitch may wander: five percent either way for anything heard in a fight, so two casts of
-- the same glyph are never the same sound; nothing for the loops.
--
-- Id is "" until the file is uploaded (scripts/upload_assets.py, docs/STUDIO_SETUP.md §7). A sound with no id is not played and
-- the client says so once at startup, naming the file. There is no fallback: what was here before was
-- the engine's own ping at nine different speeds, and a placeholder that sounds like every other game is
-- worse than silence while the real thing is being uploaded.
--
-- Everything here is generated by tools/audio/ and traced in docs/ASSETS.md. Nothing is licensed from
-- anybody.

export type SoundEntry = {
	-- "rbxassetid://123", or "" while the WAV has not been uploaded yet.
	Id: string,
	-- The file in assets/audio/ this id must be the upload of.
	Source: string,
	-- Length of that file. A layer that has to fit a window (a boss warning) is stretched from this.
	Seconds: number,
	Volume: number,
	-- Half-width of the pitch variation, as a fraction of the play speed. 0.05 is five percent either
	-- way. The generators loudness-normalise every file (RMS per voice), so Volume is a mix decision
	-- and not a correction for a quiet file.
	Vary: number,
}

